WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.767
Here are the five providers side by side,

2
00:00:02.767 --> 00:00:06.225
including Oracle Cloud,
where the HR platform runs.

3
00:00:06.225 --> 00:00:08.801
Each keeps its notices in its own place:

4
00:00:08.801 --> 00:00:11.940
Azure's Service Health
through Resource Graph,

5
00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:17.011
Microsoft 365's message center and
service health through Microsoft Graph,

6
00:00:17.011 --> 00:00:20.392
Oracle's Announcements
service, the AWS Health API,

7
00:00:20.392 --> 00:00:23.612
and Google Cloud's
Personalized Service Health.

8
00:00:23.612 --> 00:00:28.034
The least-privileged reader is
small everywhere: Reader in Azure,

9
00:00:28.034 --> 00:00:31.881
two read permissions in Graph,
a read statement in Oracle,

10
00:00:31.881 --> 00:00:36.138
three describe actions in AWS,
and a viewer role in Google Cloud.

11
00:00:36.138 --> 00:00:40.163
Only AWS has a cost: a
qualifying support plan.

12
00:00:40.163 --> 00:00:46.107
On government clouds, Microsoft 365 GCC
stays on the worldwide Graph endpoint,

13
00:00:46.107 --> 00:00:50.863
while GCC High and the Defense
Department have their own hosts.

14
00:00:50.863 --> 00:00:54.437
Oracle's US Government
Cloud has its own endpoints.

15
00:00:54.437 --> 00:00:56.576
AWS GovCloud has one.

16
00:00:56.576 --> 00:00:59.730
And Google's documentation
doesn't list Personalized

17
00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:03.100
Service Health in its FedRAMP
Moderate or High packages.
